' CoFixpoint bisim flow — the proof structure of post_gate_bisim_strong, the
' guarded coinductive construction behind the translation bisimulation. From the
' bisim_intro constructor the proof forks into a Forward arm (a W-step is matched
' by a P-step) and a Backward arm (a P-step is matched by a W-step); each arm's
' recursive call sits immediately under the bisim constructor, satisfying Rocq's
' guardedness condition.
'
' (Converted from the former Mermaid source to PlantUML; PlantUML is preferred
'  over Mermaid wherever their capabilities overlap.)
'
' Source of truth for Figure 8.1 in cost-accounted-rho-verification.md §8.1.
' Palette:  entry/hypothesis blue #BBDEFB · lemma step teal #B2DFDB ·
'           guarded RECURSE green-fill #C8E6C9 · note green #E8F5E9
'           (activity fills use the <<#hex>> stereotype-colour suffix form —
'            the #hex:label prefix form is deprecated in PlantUML 1.2026.x).
' Render:  plantuml -tsvg docs/casper/theory/diagrams/cofixpoint-bisim-flow.puml
'          (or: ./render.sh cofixpoint-bisim-flow.puml)

@startuml cofixpoint-bisim-flow
!theme plain
skinparam defaultFontName "sans-serif"
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #333333
skinparam ActivityDiamondBorderColor #444444
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #E8F5E9
skinparam NoteBorderColor #666666
title Figure 8.1 — post_gate_bisim_strong as a guarded CoFixpoint

:bisim_intro — coinductive constructor\nInputs: P, W, H : W ≡ P ∣ *(@0); <<#BBDEFB>>
note right
  W is the post-gate state: the
  original P in parallel with the
  stuck residue *(@0).
end note

fork
  -[#2E7D32]->
  :**Forward arm** — a W-step matched by a P-step;
  :W ⇝ W'   (given);
  :backward_sim_par_stuck; <<#B2DFDB>>
  :P ⇝ P'   and   W' ≡ P' ∣ *(@0);
  :RECURSE  post_gate_bisim_strong P' W' H_eq'\n(guarded — under the bisim constructor); <<#C8E6C9>>
  :P' ~~ W';
fork again
  -[#2E7D32]->
  :**Backward arm** — a P-step matched by a W-step;
  :P ⇝ P'   (given);
  :rs_par_l + rs_struct; <<#B2DFDB>>
  :W ⇝ W'   where   W' := P' ∣ *(@0);
  :RECURSE  post_gate_bisim_strong P' W' refl\n(guarded — under the bisim constructor); <<#C8E6C9>>
  :P' ~~ W';
end fork

:both arms re-enter `bisim` under its constructor\n⇒ Rocq guardedness met ⇒ productive CoFixpoint; <<#E8F5E9>>
stop

@enduml
